{{Quote|Always open! Bounty never sleeps!|Bounty Emporium's slogan|<ref name="Trivia">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/friends-and-enemies-trivia-gallery|text="Friends and Enemies" Trivia Gallery}} {{C|Slide 11}}</ref>}}
'''Bounty Emporium''' was a store for [[bounty hunter]]s active during the [[Clone Wars]]. It was established on the [[Planet|world]] of [[Orondia]],<ref name="FAE" /> as well as in [[Pons Ora]], a [[City|settlement]] on [[Abafar]].<ref name="MIA" /> It was advertised during the sporting event [[Hunters of the Outer Rim]]<ref name="Hunters" /> and on [[Arena News]].<ref name="Arena News">{{ArenaNews|url=0122de64c2544c938cd376a6e9cc75f3-en-gb|text=First Edition}}</ref>

{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Signage at the fueling station includes: Eat at Koe's, Bounty Emporium: Always Open, Bounty Never Sleeps; Security Services; Speeder Sales; The Pilot's Lounge (Live Band Every Night); Craft Repair and Maintenance; Repair Rack Droid Services; Orondia Tours; and Meteor Cafe.|StarWars.com "Friends and Enemies" Episode Guide|<ref name="Trivia" />}}
Bounty Emporium was first mentioned on a sign appearing in "[[Friends and Enemies]]," the sixteenth episode in the [[The Clone Wars: Season Four|fourth season]] of ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''. The Emporium later appeared as a building in "[[Missing in Action]]," the twelfth episode of the [[The Clone Wars: Season Five|fifth season]].

